; ted-getbchar-latin1-block-end (#362): without tokenising, getbchar
; returns a character >= $80 sign-extended, and Block Save takes it as the
; end of the block.  TED alone (no token list: tokenise off; under blitz2
; TED tokenises, and tokit clears bit 7 of the text), lines "x",
; a$="Größe":NPrint a$, "b"; block from the start of line 1 (F1) to the
; end of line 2 (BOTTOM, F2 at the start of line 3), Block Save.
; Correct: both lines with their LF in the file; the original ends the
; file after a$="Gr.
; @file bo.bas "x\na$=\"Gr\xf6\xdfe\":NPrint a$\nb"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command blitz2:ted @FILE@
; @expect data blk.txt "x\na$=\"Gr\xf6\xdfe\":NPrint a$\n"
timeout 10
wait screen
key 50
menu 2 1
key 51
menu 1 2
wait freq "Name to save block as"
freq ok "TEDRUN:work/blk.txt"
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
